</p><p>The bar chart in Figure 11 shows that Indian and Chinese were two most common non-EU+ nationalities to leave the UK in the last year. Across the two groups, study was the most common reason that originally brought them to the UK.</p><h3>Emigration of EU+ nationals</h3><p>Around 118,000 EU+ nationals are estimated to have left the UK in YE December 2025. This is broken down as follows:</p>
<ul>
  <li><p>those with status on the EU Settlement Scheme (EUSS) made up 84% (100,000)</p></li>
  <li><p>people traveling on visas made up 11% (14,000)</p></li>
  <li><p>Irish nationals made up 4% (5,000)</p></li>
</ul><p>


  

    <div class="markdown-chart-container panel--bottom-mar print--avoid-break">

      <h3 class="flush--third--vertical font-size--18 padding-top--0 margin-bottom--1">Figure 12: Those with status on the EUSS continue to account for the majority of total EU+ emigration</h3>
        
