</p><p>The stacked bar chart in Figure 12 shows that overall emigration across all three groups remained fairly stable until YE December 2025, when it decreased. People with EUSS status are consistently the majority of EU+ emigration. This is because a large majority of EU citizens living in the UK have this status, because they arrived before the end of 2020.</p><p>


  

    <div class="markdown-chart-container panel--bottom-mar print--avoid-break">

